	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["75B7246A1B0C350B"]
			description: [
				"&c&lThe Aether.&r Your sky island is not the only world - but the old doors are sealed, and space holds most of the keys."
				""
				"&7The Aether&r needs no planet at all - glowstone and a bucket of water will open it. Its &edungeons&r are the gate, not its door."
				"&7The Undergarden&r demands a catalyst cored with &eMars&r ostrum."
				"&7The Everbright&r ignites only with a lighter forged from &eVenus&r calorite."
				""
				"Climb the solar system and two of the three dimensions fall open behind you. The Aether is open from the first day - but its bosses guard the keys your endgame demands."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:ender_pearl"
			id: "7EF5DDBB65C58DDC"
			rewards: [{
				id: "0B10E0765D673687"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 3
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7One planet, one realm"
			tasks: [{
				id: "602BD00C67B592FA"
				title: "Beyond the Island"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Realms Beyond"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7EF5DDBB65C58DDC"]
			description: [
				"Build a frame of &eGlowstone&r - any shape a Nether portal would accept - and fill it with a &ebucket of water&r. The surface shimmers, and you fall &lupward&r."
				""
				"&aNo gate, no planet, no boss.&r The Aether is the one dimension you can reach on day one. That is deliberate: the Aether is where you go to &lget&r strong, not a reward for already being strong."
				""
				"&e&lWhat you are walking into:&r an endless sky of floating islands, Holystone and Aercloud, with three dungeons buried in it - &6Bronze&r, &7Silver&r and &eGold&r. Each is sealed by a boss, and each boss drops exactly one key."
				""
				"&c&lThose four keys are the pack's ending.&r Bronze, Silver, Gold and Deep Aether's Brass are four of the five components of the &bCelestial Core&r. Do not spend them casually."
				""
				"&8Falling off the edge of the Aether does not kill you - it drops you back into the overworld. In a skyblock, that means falling into the void. Bring blocks."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:glowstone"
			id: "67BC6ABF61224134"
			rewards: [{
				count: 16
				id: "2EB10EA25CB53217"
				item: "minecraft:glowstone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&aOpen from the start - no gate"
			tasks: [{
				dimension: "aether:the_aether"
				id: "4BA53916264ABFE6"
				type: "dimension"
			}]
			title: "Into the Aether"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["67BC6ABF61224134"]
			description: [
				"The &6Slider&r sleeps inside the Bronze Dungeon, buried under the islands. Wake it and the room becomes the fight."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the Aether's tutorial boss&r - and the first Celestial Core component. Killing it drops the &6Bronze Key&r. &lKeep the key.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThe fight:&r an animated stone cube that slams along the axes of its chamber, ricocheting between the walls. It does not chase you the way a mob does - it lines up and fires itself."
				"&7- &fMove diagonally.&7 It can only travel along one axis at a time, so a corner is the safest place in the room."
				"&7- &fHit it when it stops.&7 It pauses to re-aim between slams - that window is your entire damage output."
				"&7- &fDo not melee it while it is moving&7; you will be crushed against the wall."
				"&7- &fThe chamber is sealed&7 until it dies. There is no retreating, so bring food and a shield in with you."
				""
				"&e&lDrops:&r the &6Bronze Dungeon Key&r and Carved Stone. The dungeon's reward chest holds Zanite gear, the Hammer of Kingbdogz and the Agility Cape."
				""
				"&8Iron gear is genuinely enough here if you respect the corners. This is the friendliest boss in the chapter - the difficulty climbs steeply after it."
			]
			icon: "aether:bronze_dungeon_key"
			id: "321DE9424210F3F1"
			rewards: [{
				count: 6
				id: "51A7A36D2BE9D256"
				item: "aether:zanite_gemstone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Bronze Key - Core component one"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "aether:slider"
				id: "0481725F962E0ED5"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			title: "The Slider"
			x: -4.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["321DE9424210F3F1"]
			description: [
				"The &7Valkyrie Queen&r holds the Silver Dungeon - and she will not so much as look at you until you have earned the right to ask."
				""
				"&c&lThis kill unlocks Draconic Evolution.&r The &bDraconium Core&r - the root of the entire Draconic tree and therefore all of Act IV - is now pinned with the &7Silver Dungeon Key&r. No Valkyrie Queen, no Draconic."
				""
				"&e&lYou cannot simply attack her.&r Talk to her and she demands &7Victory Medals&r - dropped by the ordinary Valkyries patrolling the dungeon. Kill enough of them, hand the medals over, and only then does the fight begin. The dungeon crawl IS the boss gate."
				""
				"&e&lThe fight:&r she flies, teleports, and hits far harder than anything you have met. Her Valkyries do not join in, but the arena is open and she uses all of it."
				"&7- &fShe closes distance instantly.&7 Ranged will not save you - expect melee."
				"&7- &fFight her on the ground&7 where you can strafe; do not get cornered against the arena walls."
				"&7- &fBring golden apples.&7 Her burst damage is the highest so far in the pack."
				""
				"&e&lDrops:&r the &7Silver Dungeon Key&r. The reward chest holds the Holy Sword, Invisibility Cloak and Enchanted Gravitite. &lKeep the key.&r"
				""
				"&8Clear the Valkyries first and bank the medals before you commit. Dying mid-negotiation means walking the whole dungeon again."
			]
			icon: "aether:silver_dungeon_key"
			id: "7194AE474BDDA510"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "7D6E4A4E7E1C768C"
				item: "aether:golden_amber"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&cSilver Key gates Draconic"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "aether:valkyrie_queen"
				id: "219FACD6690D1306"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			title: "The Valkyrie Queen"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7194AE474BDDA510"]
			description: [
				"At the bottom of the Gold Dungeon, in a hall of fire, waits the &eSun Spirit&r - the Aether's final boss."
				""
				"&c&lThis fight pays for wireless AE2.&r The &eGold Dungeon Key&r is the frame of the &bQuantum Ring&r - the block that links your island network to the Moon, Mars and everywhere else. It is also Celestial Core component three."
				""
				"&e&lThe fight is a puzzle, not a slugfest.&r He is immune to your weapons. He hovers, laughing, and throws fire while summoning Fire Minions."
				"&7- &fHe can only be hurt by snowballs.&7 Bring stacks of them - this is not a joke, it is the entire mechanic."
				"&7- &fThe arena is lava-floored.&7 Fire resistance is close to mandatory and a single knockback can end the run."
				"&7- &fKill the Fire Minions&7 or they will chip you to death while you are aiming."
				"&7- &fIcestone from the Aether&7 makes snowballs renewable - stock up before you go down."
				""
				"&e&lDrops:&r the &eGold Dungeon Key&r and the &7Sun Altar&r, which lets you set the Aether's time of day forever after. The reward chest holds Gravitite gear, the Vampire Blade and Life Shards."
				""
				"&8Beating him permanently ends the Aether's eternal-day cycle if you want it to. Come with your best armour, fire resistance, and more snowballs than you think you need."
			]
			icon: "aether:gold_dungeon_key"
			id: "10583B7DED57F345"
